# netsurf: a real canvas 2D context -- shapes, strokes, text, images,
# gradients, clipping, getImageData / putImageData, toDataURL (patch 251);
# a display:none <img> loads, and window load waits for it
# Generated 2026-10-11
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 250)
#
# getContext('2d') returned a context whose every drawing method did
# nothing (fixes1245): charts, games, maps, QR codes, avatars and the
# image grid of a captcha were blank, and a script reading back its own
# drawing (getImageData, toDataURL -- fingerprinting, hCaptcha) got zeros
# or a fixed 1x1 PNG. Chromium draws all of it.
#
#  - quickjs/macsurf_canvas.c (new): the pixels. Each context keeps
#    premultiplied RGBA in ordinary memory; the changed rectangle is copied
#    unpremultiplied into the element's bitmap (the canvas node's
#    __ns_key_canvas_node_data user data, which redraw.c already plots for
#    a canvas box) from a scheduled callback, once per batch of drawing,
#    and the box is redrawn. Shapes arrive flattened to polygons in device
#    pixels; a scanline rasteriser samples 4 sub-scanlines per row with
#    exact horizontal coverage, nonzero or even-odd. A stroke is the union
#    of convex pieces (a quad per segment; miter / bevel / round joins;
#    butt / square / round caps), all wound the same way so the nonzero
#    rule merges them. Paints: colour, linear / radial / conic gradients
#    (256-entry table), images (drawImage and patterns) sampled through
#    the inverse transform, nearest or bilinear. Porter-Duff operators,
#    lighter, multiply, screen, darken, lighten; the clip is a coverage
#    mask saved and restored with the state. PNG export uses stored
#    deflate blocks. Coordinates are clamped before every float/int
#    conversion (ASan + UBSan clean over 60 000 fuzzed native calls).
#  - vita_polyfill.js: CanvasRenderingContext2D -- styles, transforms,
#    the path (points transformed as they are added, curves and arcs
#    flattened in device pixels), Path2D with SVG path data, line dashes,
#    CSS colours (named, hex, rgb/rgba, hsl/hsla) and fonts, gradients,
#    patterns, ImageData, measureText, isPointInPath / isPointInStroke,
#    canvas width / height (setting either clears the canvas and resets
#    the context), toDataURL / toBlob, createImageBitmap. Colours are
#    parsed once per string; fillRect avoids the path builder.
#  - text: the frontend renders glyphs with FreeType straight into the
#    canvas (vita_text_glyphs, not through the screen's glyph atlas), in
#    the page's own faces, so measureText and fillText agree.
#  - drawImage(<img>): html_image_bitmap() -- the box's object, or the
#    image a detached <img> (new Image()) loaded, which is now kept
#    decoded (24 per page at most, oldest returned to the cache first).
#  - A display:none <img> never loaded (no box, no object fetch): no load
#    event, naturalWidth 0, nothing for drawImage of a hidden sprite
#    sheet. Box construction now fetches it as a detached image does
#    (html_image_fetch_hidden, once per URL; not loading=lazy), counted in
#    the page's active fetches so window load waits for it as in browsers.
#
# Not done: shadows, filters, text rotated or skewed by the transform
# (glyphs stay upright at the transformed origin and size), strokeText
# draws filled glyphs.
#
# Gate: testpages/pages/JS-canvas-2d.html, CANVAS251 22/22 (Chromium
# 22/22): every check reads pixels back; plus the page's own canvas on
# screen (run-vita-sim.sh reads the snapshot under its plotted bitmap).
